# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# Only these paths get a real prerendered file at build time (see
# scripts/generate-static-pages.mjs): /, /docs, /blog and each blog post.
# Every other route is client-side only — App.tsx switches on
# window.location.pathname — so a static host must serve index.html for them or
# a direct hit / refresh / shared link 404s.
#
# Routes are listed EXPLICITLY rather than using a blanket `/* / 200`, so a
# path that does not exist (/api/*, /mcp, a mistyped URL) is a real 404 rather
# than the SPA shell with a 200. Add a line here when you add a route to
# App.tsx that isn't prerendered.
#
# The rewrite target is `/`, NOT `/index.html`. Pages canonicalises HTML paths
# ("pretty URLs": /about/index.html → /about/), so a 200 rewrite to /index.html
# hits that canonicalisation and comes back to the browser as a 308 with
# `Location: /`, i.e. every direct hit on /trust, /terms, … landed on the
# homepage. Rewriting to `/` serves the same root index.html with a 200 and
# leaves the URL alone, so App.tsx sees the real path.

/trust              /   200
/metrics-reference  /   200
/terms              /   200
/privacy            /   200
